# Old Webflow URLs -> the new site. Crawled from the live eleveno.com on
# 2026-08-25; that site is a closed set of 8 pages with nothing deeper.
# 301 = permanent, which is what passes the old page's search ranking on.
# Netlify matches these top-down, so order matters.

/about              /                       301
/partners           /#partners              301
/eat-and-drink      /menu-food.html         301
/private-events     /private-events.html    301

# /pickleball, /privacy-policy and /terms-and-conditions need no rule: each
# now has a page of the same name, and Netlify serves pickleball.html for the
# extensionless path, so those old Webflow URLs keep resolving on their own.

# The beer garden is closed for the season, not gone. 302 (temporary) on
# purpose: a 301 would tell Google to drop the URL, and the page comes back
# in spring — restore the whole thing with `git revert` of the removal commit.
/beer-garden        /                       302
